// Int literals are signed 64-bit. This one is one past `i64::MAX`, so the walker rejects it
// while building the AST — the grammar itself is happy with any run of digits.
//
// The width is deliberate: it used to be `usize`, which is 32-bit under
// `wasm32-unknown-unknown`, so a literal this size parsed fine natively and trapped in the
// browser. Pinning the boundary here keeps that divergence from coming back.
9223372036854775808
